    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option C (\"Incentivize solo commuter motorists to transition towards public transport networks\")\n\n• Acoustic & Textual Evidence:\nThe audio recording explicitly states: \"Civic Mobility. Starting October 1st, the regional transit authority is rolling out its single monthly pass priced at 49 dollars. Valid without restriction across the entire commuter rail network as well as suburban coaches, this measure aims to persuade single-occupancy drivers to forgo highway gridlock during peak hours.\".\nChoice C accurately expresses the key information verified in the audio recording.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options & Refutations):\n  - Option A (\"Cap the daily ceiling of transit ridership during peak morning commuting rushes\") [INCORRECT - SURFACE LEXICAL ECHO TRAP]: Unsubstantiated inference: while related vocabulary appears in the audio, it does not support concluding \"Cap the daily ceiling of transit ridership during peak morning commuting rushes\".\n  - Option B (\"Fund the physical widening of tolled highways into remote agricultural zones\") [INCORRECT - UNWARRANTED EXTRAPOLATION TRAP]: Unsubstantiated inference: while related vocabulary appears in the audio, it does not support concluding \"Fund the physical widening of tolled highways into remote agricultural zones\".\n  - Option C (\"Incentivize solo commuter motorists to transition towards public transport networks\") [CORRECT]: Accurately reflects the verified facts in the recording and directly answers the question asked.\n  - Option D (\"Phase out human bus operators in favor of autonomous self-driving shuttles\") [INCORRECT - SURFACE LEXICAL ECHO TRAP]: Unsubstantiated inference: while related vocabulary appears in the audio, it does not support concluding \"Phase out human bus operators in favor of autonomous self-driving shuttles\"."
